{"chunk_id": "1e966229d3bb", "text": "This chapter centers on Parvati\u2019s unwavering devotion to Shiva and the divine test that proves her worthiness. After the sages report her steadfast penance, Shiva disguises himself as an old monk to test her resolve. Parvati welcomes him but remains firm in her vow to marry Shiva alone, even attempting to enter fire when she believes her penance has failed\u2014yet the fire turns cool, showing divine favor. When the disguised Shiva insults himself to provoke her, Parvati passionately defends the true nature of Shiva as the supreme Absolute. Satisfied, Shiva reveals himself and promises union. Their love continues through playful divine disguises and cosmic displays, while sages persuade Parvati\u2019s parents to approve the wedding. The episode highlights bhakti, the metaphysical identity of Shiva with the Absolute, and the triumph of pure devotion over doubt and social convention.\nParvati proves her unwavering devotion to Siva, passes his disguised test, gains his acceptance, and preparations begin for their formal marriage.\nThemes: devotion and penance, divine testing, union of Siva and Parvati, nature of the Absolute, marriage and dharma", "vector": [0.015010139904916286, -0.022022077813744545, -0.0037998214829713106, 0.011348800733685493, -0.002572057070210576, 0.014861524105072021, -0.01444269996136427, -0.017117774114012718, -0.026507554575800896, -0.03153345361351967, 0.01705022156238556, 0.02831795997917652, 0.004593562334775925, 0.0038268426433205605, -0.012693093158304691, 0.011855443008244038, 0.048124317079782486, 0.0009769763564690948, 0.0252105500549078, -0.029236672446131706, -0.003587031504139304, -0.005282596219331026, -0.018725519999861717, 0.0018745786510407925, -0.03453277796506882, -0.007809055503457785, 0.01822563260793686, -0.03177664056420326, 0.011071835644543171, -0.008829096332192421, -0.01371313352137804, -0.00793740525841713, -0.02581852115690708, -0.04520605504512787, -0.012105387635529041, -